## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to simplify tagging, maintain per-env isolation, and introduce a safe migration path.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform provider default_tags
- Per-env backend prefixes
- Gate checks on plan output for tag presence
- Migration risk and rollback considerations

## Code Example
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
  default_tags = {
    tags = {
      Environment = var.environment
      CostCenter  = var.cost_center
    }
  }
}
```

```hcl
# migrated resource sample (no wrapper)
resource "aws_vpc" "main" { cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16" }
```

```hcl
# backend example
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "corp-terraform-state"
    key    = "envs/${var.environment}/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle prod tag overrides if needed?
- What tooling would you add to enforce tag presence across environments?

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses practical multi-cloud Terraform coordination, provider aliasing, per-cloud backends, and gating across tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-cloud provider configuration with aliasing
- Per-cloud backends and remote state isolation
- CI gates that validate plans across clouds
- Enforcing region constraints and mandatory tagging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton Terraform-like snippet demonstrating provider aliases and cloud map
variable "cloud" { type = string; description = "aws or gcp" }

provider "aws" {
  region = lookup(var.cloud_map, var.cloud, {})["aws_region"]
}
provider "google" {
  region = lookup(var.cloud_map, var.cloud, {})["gcp_region"]
}

module "tenant_network" {
  source = "./modules/network"
  cloud  = var.cloud
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale adding additional clouds?
- How would you verify tagging and cost-center propagation across tenants?
